<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 243 0 R
/E (Airlines receive thousands of tweets every day, and there is no scalable solution for processing them. This creates a significant backlog, as manual reviews are slow and prone to bias, ultimately resulting in critical patterns being overlooked. Valuable customer feedback is wasted, which could otherwise inform service improvements and enhance customer satisfaction.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
283 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 243 0 R
/E (The Problem)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 243 0 R
/E (We propose an end-to-end NLP pipeline that classifies every tweet as Negative, Neutral, or Positive. By utilizing supervised Logistic Regression and unsupervised K-Means clustering, we can efficiently analyze sentiment in real-time. This approach allows airlines to harness customer feedback proactively, driving improvements in service and addressing passenger complaints effectively.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
